The current approach uses `exitProcess(0)` which is not ideal. A better approach would be to use a combination of flags that properly restart the app without killing the process abruptly. 

Common alternatives include:
1. Using `FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TASK` along with `FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK` to properly restart the activity stack
2. Using `Runtime.getRuntime().exit(0)` (but still not ideal)
3. Using `Process.killProcess(Process.myPid())` (also not ideal)
